cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use AMFsplit, please cite the archived release and the application note."
title: "AMFsplit: reproducible naming of arbuscular mycorrhizal fungi from linked long-read rRNA sequences"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "O'Brien"
    given-names: "Aaron"
license: "MIT"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ayobi/amfsplit"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23966769"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-11-04"
abstract: >-
  Names long-read rRNA gene sequences of arbuscular mycorrhizal fungi by MaarjAM virtual taxon, UNITE
  species hypothesis and LSU species clade with the culture-linked method of O'Brien, Marín and Tedersoo,
  reproducing its published calls byte for byte, and reports how far each call can be trusted. Fixes
  proposed since that study ship as opt-in rules, to be adopted only after Protocol v3, a pre-registered
  test whose protocol, rule code and predictions were locked on 4 November 2026
  (doi:10.5281/zenodo.23962473).
keywords:
  - arbuscular mycorrhizal fungi
  - rRNA genes
  - long reads
  - metabarcoding
  - taxonomic assignment
  - novelty detection
  - reproducibility
preferred-citation:
